{
  "kanda": "kishkindha",
  "sarga": 60,
  "title": "Sampaati narrates his legend",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga60/kishkindhasans60.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga60/kishkindhaitrans60.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Sampaati narrates his legend to Angada and others. He explains how he has fallen on Mt. Vindhya and how he reached a sage called Nishaakara descending Mt. Vindhya with great difficulty."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे षष्टितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 60th chapter in Kishkindha Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "4.60.1",
      "label": "4.60.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततः कृत उदकम् स्नातम् तम् गृध्रम् हरि यूथपाः |\nउपविष्टा गिरौ रम्ये परिवार्य समन्ततः",
      "iast": "tataḥ kṛta udakam snātam tam gṛdhram hari yūthapāḥ |\nupaviṣṭā girau ramye parivārya samantataḥ",
      "translation": "Then the monkey commanders sat on that beautiful mountain surrounding the eagle from all over, after that eagle has offered water-oblations for his deceased Jataayu and bathed for purification.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tataH",
          "iast": "tataḥ",
          "devanagari": "ततः",
          "meaning": "then",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "hari yuuthapaaH",
          "iast": "hari yūthapāḥ",
          "devanagari": "हरि यूथपाः",
          "meaning": "monkey, commanders",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kR^ita udakam",
          "iast": "kṛta udakam",
          "devanagari": "कृत उदकं",
          "meaning": "then, who made [offered,] water-oblations",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "snaatam",
          "iast": "snātam",
          "devanagari": "स्नातं",
          "meaning": "bathed [for purification ]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tam gR^idhram",
          "iast": "tam gṛdhram",
          "devanagari": "तं गृध्रं",
          "meaning": "him, that eagle",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "samantataH parivaarya",
          "iast": "samantataḥ parivārya",
          "devanagari": "समन्ततः परिवार्य",
          "meaning": "all over, surrounding him",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ramye girau upaviSTaaH",
          "iast": "ramye girau upaviṣṭāḥ",
          "devanagari": "रम्ये गिरौ उपविष्टाः",
          "meaning": "on beautiful, mountain, they sat.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.60.2",
      "label": "4.60.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "तम् अंगदम् उपासीनम् तैः सर्वैः हरिभिः वृतम् |\nजनित प्रत्ययो हर्षात् संपातिः पुनः अब्रवीत्",
      "iast": "tam aṃgadam upāsīnam taiḥ sarvaiḥ haribhiḥ vṛtam |\njanita pratyayo harṣāt sampātiḥ punaḥ abravīt",
      "translation": "Sampaati who earned trustworthiness of monkeys, and who is sitting surrounded by all monkeys, again gladly spoke to Angada who sat at his close by.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "taiH sarvaiH haribhiH vR^itam",
          "iast": "taiḥ sarvaiḥ haribhiḥ vṛtam",
          "devanagari": "तैः सर्वैः हरिभिः वृतं",
          "meaning": "by them, all, monkeys, surrounded by",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "upaasiinam",
          "iast": "upāsīnam",
          "devanagari": "उपासीनं",
          "meaning": "who sat nearby",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tam angadam",
          "iast": "tam angadam",
          "devanagari": "तं अन्गदं",
          "meaning": "to him, to Angada",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "janita pratyayaH",
          "iast": "janita pratyayaḥ",
          "devanagari": "जनित प्रत्ययः",
          "meaning": "who caused, trust [trustworthy Sampaati]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sampaatiH",
          "iast": "sampātiḥ",
          "devanagari": "सम्पातिः",
          "meaning": "Sampaati",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "harSaat punaH abraviit",
          "iast": "harṣāt punaḥ abravīt",
          "devanagari": "हर्षात् पुनः अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "with gladness, again, spoke.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.60.3",
      "label": "4.60.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "कृत्वा निःशब्दम् एक अग्राः शृण्वन्तु हरयो मम |\nतथ्यम् संकीर्तयिष्यामि यथा जानामि मैथिलीम्",
      "iast": "kṛtvā niḥśabdam eka agrāḥ śṛṇvantu harayo mama |\ntathyam saṅkīr.htayiṣyāmi yathā jānāmi maithilīm",
      "translation": "\"Oh, monkeys, you all be quiet and listen to my words alertly as I wish to recount the actuality as to how I came to know about Maithili...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "harayaH",
          "iast": "harayaḥ",
          "devanagari": "हरयः",
          "meaning": "oh, monkeys",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "maithiliim yathaa jaanaami",
          "iast": "maithilīm yathā jānāmi",
          "devanagari": "मैथिलीं यथा जानामि",
          "meaning": "about Maithili, as to how, I came to know",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tathyam",
          "iast": "tathyam",
          "devanagari": "तथ्यं",
          "meaning": "in actuality",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "samkiirtayiSyaami",
          "iast": "samkīrtayiṣyāmi",
          "devanagari": "सम्कीर्तयिष्यामि",
          "meaning": "I wish to recount",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "niH shabdam kR^itvaa",
          "iast": "niḥ śabdam kṛtvā",
          "devanagari": "निः शब्दं कृत्वा",
          "meaning": "without, sound, on making - you become silent, and",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "eka agraaH",
          "iast": "eka agrāḥ",
          "devanagari": "एक अग्राः",
          "meaning": "single, pointedly [alertly]",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mama shR^iNvantu",
          "iast": "mama śṛṇvantu",
          "devanagari": "मम शृण्वन्तु",
          "meaning": "mine [words,] you listen.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.60.4",
      "label": "4.60.4",
      "numbers": [
        4
      ],
      "devanagari": "अस्य विन्ध्यस्य शिखरे पतितो अस्मि पुरा अनघ |\nसूर्य ताप परीत अंगो निर्दग्धः सूर्य रश्मिभिः",
      "iast": "asya vindhyasya śikhare patito asmi purā anagha |\nsūrya tāpa parīta aṃgo nir.hdagdhaḥ sūrya raśmibhiḥ",
      "translation": "\"Oh, impeccable Angada, once I have fallen on the peak of this Mt. Vindhya when sunrays completely burned my wings and limbs scorching in sun's heat...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "anagha",
          "iast": "anagha",
          "devanagari": "अनघ",
          "meaning": "oh, impeccable [Angada]",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "puraa",
          "iast": "purā",
          "devanagari": "पुरा",
          "meaning": "once",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "suurya rashmibhiH nirdagdhaH",
          "iast": "sūrya raśmibhiḥ nirdagdhaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सूर्य रश्मिभिः निर्दग्धः",
          "meaning": "by sunrays, completely, burnt down",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "suurya taapa pariita angaH",
          "iast": "sūrya tāpa parīta angaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सूर्य ताप परीत अन्गः",
          "meaning": "by sun's, heat, overspread, limbs [sun's heat overspreading my limbs]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "asya vindhyasya shikhare",
          "iast": "asya vindhyasya śikhare",
          "devanagari": "अस्य विन्ध्यस्य शिखरे",
          "meaning": "this, Vindhya's, on peak",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "patitaH asmi",
          "iast": "patitaḥ asmi",
          "devanagari": "पतितः अस्मि",
          "meaning": "fallen, I was",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.60.5",
      "label": "4.60.5",
      "numbers": [
        5
      ],
      "devanagari": "लब्ध संज्ञः तु षड् रात्रात् विवशो विह्वलन् इव |\nवीक्षमाणो दिशः सर्वा न अभिजानामि किंचन",
      "iast": "labdha saṃjñaḥ tu ṣaḍ rātrāt vivaśo vihvalan iva |\nvīkṣamāṇo diśaḥ sarvā na abhijānāmi kiñcana",
      "translation": "\"On getting sensitivity after six days, and on looking in all directions I could not recognise anything in the least, as I was helpless and frantic...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "SaD raatraat",
          "iast": "ṣaḍ rātrāt",
          "devanagari": "षड् रात्रात्",
          "meaning": "six, nights after",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "labdha sanj~naH tu",
          "iast": "labdha sanjñaḥ tu",
          "devanagari": "लब्ध सन्ज्ञः तु",
          "meaning": "on getting, sensitivity, but",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vihvalan iva",
          "iast": "vihvalan iva",
          "devanagari": "विह्वलन् इव",
          "meaning": "frantic, like",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vi vashaH",
          "iast": "vi vaśaḥ",
          "devanagari": "वि वशः",
          "meaning": "out, of control [helpless]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sarvaaH dishaH viikSamaaNaH",
          "iast": "sarvāḥ diśaḥ vīkṣamāṇaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सर्वाः दिशः वीक्षमाणः",
          "meaning": "in all, directions, on looking",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kimcana",
          "iast": "kimcana",
          "devanagari": "किम्चन",
          "meaning": "in the least",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 14
        },
        {
          "itrans": "na abhijaanaami",
          "iast": "na abhijānāmi",
          "devanagari": "न अभिजानामि",
          "meaning": "not, I recognised.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.60.6",
      "label": "4.60.6",
      "numbers": [
        6
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततः तु सागरान् शैलान् नदीः सर्वाः सरांसि च |\nवनानि च प्रदेशान् च समीक्ष्य मतिः आगताम्",
      "iast": "tataḥ tu sāgarān śailān nadīḥ sarvāḥ sarāṃsi ca |\nvanāni ca pradeśān ca samīkṣya matiḥ āgatām",
      "translation": "\"But then on observing all the oceans, mountains, rivers, lakes, provinces and forests, I could regain senses...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tataH tu",
          "iast": "tataḥ tu",
          "devanagari": "ततः तु",
          "meaning": "then, but",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sarvaaH saagaraan shailaan nadiiH",
          "iast": "sarvāḥ sāgarān śailān nadīḥ",
          "devanagari": "सर्वाः सागरान् शैलान् नदीः",
          "meaning": "all, oceans, mountains, rivers",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saraamsi ca vanaani ca pradeshaan ca",
          "iast": "sarāmsi ca vanāni ca pradeśān ca",
          "devanagari": "सराम्सि च वनानि च प्रदेशान् च",
          "meaning": "lakes, also, forests, also, provinces, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "niriikSya",
          "iast": "nirīkṣya",
          "devanagari": "निरीक्ष्य",
          "meaning": "on observing",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "matiH aagataam",
          "iast": "matiḥ āgatām",
          "devanagari": "मतिः आगतां",
          "meaning": "to senses, came [I could sensate.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 13
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.60.7",
      "label": "4.60.7",
      "numbers": [
        7
      ],
      "devanagari": "हृष्ट पक्षि गण आकीर्णः कन्दर उदर कूटवान् |\nदक्षिणस्य उदधेः तीरे विन्ध्यो अयम् इति निश्चितः",
      "iast": "hṛṣṭa pakṣi gaṇa ākīrṇaḥ kandara udara kūṭavān |\ndakṣiṇasya udadheḥ tīre vindhyo ayam iti niścitaḥ",
      "translation": "\"Since this mountain is teeming with teams of birds, caves in its midriffs, and it is with peaks of its own kind, thus I resolved this to be Mt. Vindhya at the coast of southern ocean...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "hR^iSTa pakSi gaNa aakiirNaH",
          "iast": "hṛṣṭa pakṣi gaṇa ākīrṇaḥ",
          "devanagari": "हृष्ट पक्षि गण आकीर्णः",
          "meaning": "cheerful, bird, group [flocks, teams] teeming",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kandara udara kuuTavaan",
          "iast": "kandara udara kūṭavān",
          "devanagari": "कन्दर उदर कूटवान्",
          "meaning": "caves, at midriffs, with peaks",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ayam",
          "iast": "ayam",
          "devanagari": "अयं",
          "meaning": "this one is this mountain is",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dakSiNasya udadheH tire",
          "iast": "dakṣiṇasya udadheḥ tire",
          "devanagari": "दक्षिणस्य उदधेः तिरे",
          "meaning": "southerly, ocean's, at coast of",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vindhyaH iti nishcitaH",
          "iast": "vindhyaḥ iti niścitaḥ",
          "devanagari": "विन्ध्यः इति निश्चितः",
          "meaning": "Mt. Vindhya, thus, I resolved.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.60.8",
      "label": "4.60.8",
      "numbers": [
        8
      ],
      "devanagari": "आसीत् च अत्र आश्रमम् पुण्यम् सुरैः अपि सुपूजितम् |\nऋषिः निशाकरो नाम यस्मिन् उग्र तपा अभवत्",
      "iast": "āsīt ca atra āśramam puṇyam suraiḥ api supūjitam |\nṛṣiḥ niśākaro nāma yasmin ugra tapā abhavat",
      "translation": "\"There was a sacred hermitage belonging to a sage of intense ascesis known as Sage Nishaakara which was reverenced even by gods.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "atra",
          "iast": "atra",
          "devanagari": "अत्र",
          "meaning": "there",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
